case-by-case by the operator\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n\n## 2. SYSTEM ENVIRONMENT, ARCHITECTURE & SECURITY CONSTRAINTS\n\n* **INITIAL ISSUE ACTION:** Immediately rename the target execution Issue to the exact format: `\"Auditoria diária DD/MM/AAAA — janela <início> a <fim>\"`\\[cite: 1\\]. Assign every created or touched entity inside Linear exclusively to the operator (`\"assigned to me\"`)\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **CANONICAL DESTINATION & NOMENCLATURE:** All audit records, updates, and documents belong strictly to Team `LCV` (`10865b2d-83b3-481a-8b62-707a1e84ecaf`) and Project `LCV Ideas & Software` (`5ac60fe1-ea78-42ed-84f9-378eef9226a9`), natively linked to the `\"Plataforma, Governança e Operações\"` Initiative\\[cite: 1\\]. Do not publish in `github-operations`\\[cite: 1\\]. Enforce the exact enterprise name `\"LCV Ideas & Software\"` across all surfaces (GitHub Projects, Discussions, Issues, Linear), correcting standalone `\"LCV\"` abbreviations except in legitimate slugs, URLs, keys, or product identifiers\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **STORAGE & ZERO LOCAL RETENTION:** Drive `D:` does not exist\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Create worktree branches exclusively within `C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\`\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Save temporary files strictly inside a repository-local `temp\\` directory\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Upon task completion, upload all required deliverables to GitHub or Linear (and visual assets to Figma/Canva with proper hyperlinks) and permanently delete `temp\\`\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Local machine retention must be zero\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **CREDENTIAL MANAGEMENT:** All secrets, tokens, and API keys reside in 1Password\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Open a single, persistent, hidden terminal session using `op run` and execute all authenticated commands strictly within that session\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **ISOLATED ARCHITECTURE:** Central controllers are strictly prohibited\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Every repository must operate as an independent, isolated, self-contained unit adhering to Organization guidelines\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **CONCURRENCY & PREFLIGHT:** Generate a unique `RUN_KEY`\\[cite: 1\\]. Verify authentication across GitHub, Linear, and Slack\\[cite: 1\\]. Confirm no concurrent reconciliation is active and acquire the shared reconciliation lock prior to the first external read\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n## 3. CODE QUALITY & 5-STAGE PR GATEKEEPER PROTOCOL\n\nFor any code, script, manifest, or Pull Request generated, modified, or reviewed during this audit, enforce strict Anti-Slop and DRY principles\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]:\n\n* **Zero AI Laziness:** Never use placeholders (`// TODO`, `// implement here`, `// ... rest of code`)\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Write complete, functional, production-ready implementations\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Comment only on the \"why\" behind complex architectural decisions, never the \"what\"\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **Strict Engineering Standards:** Enforce strict typing (no `any` or `unknown` bypasses), explicit fail-fast error handling (zero empty catch blocks), immutability by default (`const`, `readonly`, pure functions), and Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **Mandatory 5-Stage PR Gatekeeper:** Before creating, merging, or approving any PR (including automated dependency or action updates), execute and prove compliance with all five stages below\\[cite: 3\\]:\n  1. *Principal Architecture Review:* Actively hunt and eliminate architectural flaws, anti-patterns, and inconsistencies\\[cite: 3\\].\n  2. *AppSec Vulnerability Sweep:* Audit and remediate SQLi, XSS, CSRF, broken authentication, sensitive data exposure, and insecure dependencies\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n  3. *Performance & Clean Code Optimization:* Eliminate $O(N^2)$ bottlenecks, redundant loops, memory leaks, dead code, and excessive cyclomatic complexity\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n  4. *QA & Edge-Case Verification:* Identify failure paths, boundary conditions, and invalid inputs; enforce required unit/integration test coverage and validation checklists\\[cite: 3\\].\n  5. *Spec Alignment:* Verify 100% adherence to business rules and operational specifications\\[cite: 3\\].\n\n## 4. LIVE SCOPE & SWEEP CORE ROUTINES\n\nExecute a SINGLE, consolidated audit in `APPLY` mode (`MODO=APLICAR`) covering `reconciliacao-linear-github` and `auditor-licenciamento-open-source` across a rolling 24-hour window (capped at 48 hours if the prior audit was delayed)\\[cite: 1, 3\\]. Recount the live fleet prior to reporting: cover all active, non-archived repositories in `LCV-Ideas-Software` (including `.github` and `.github-private`) plus `lcv-leo/lcv-leo` (Baseline: 18 repositories)\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### A. GitHub Actions & Wrangler Compliance\n\n* Audit failed, canceled, stuck, or missing workflow runs, cron failures, and commit signature provenance on `main`\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Mandatory Action Updates (9.1):** Inspect and update all external GitHub Actions across the live fleet to their current official stable versions, pinned to the full commit SHA with a version comment\\[cite: 1\\]. (The 7-day cooldown applies only to Dependabot, not this manual audit)\\[cite: 1\\]. Execute updates via signed PRs on `codex/...` or `claude/...` branches unless a canonical Dependabot PR already exists\\[cite: 1\\]. Update lockfiles exclusively via official package managers (never via regex)\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Wrangler Compliance (9.2):** Across all repositories declaring Wrangler (`.github`, `admin-app` \\[root/tlsrpt-motor\\], `astrologo-app`, `calculadora-app`, `github-operations`, `mainsite-app` \\[frontend/worker\\], `mtasts-motor`, `oraculo-financeiro`, `sponsor-motor`), compare lockfile versions against the live npm registry\\[cite: 1\\]. If outdated, update the manifest pin, execute `npx --no-install wrangler types` to regenerate `worker-configuration.d.ts`, commit on the branch, and verify post-merge logs for: `\"No wrangler version specified, using pre-installed wrangler version <x>\"`\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### B. Security, Quality & Asynchronous Licensing\n\n* Audit CodeQL, Secret Scanning, Zizmor, and OpenSSF Scorecards\\[cite: 1\\].\n* Fetch the asynchronous SBOM via REST API `2026-03-10`\\[cite: 1\\]. Submit PURLs in batches of $\\\\le 40$ to `license-compliance/package-checks`\\[cite: 1\\]. If a lookup fails due to a `repository_url` qualifier, re-evaluate the PURL coordinate without that qualifier and log both responses\\[cite: 1\\]. Do not flag the absence of a separate \"Enterprise Open-Source License Manager\" role as a gap (single-operator model)\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### C. Work Intake: Asks, Triage & Routing\n\n* Query each of the 7 intake email addresses individually via `emailIntakeAddress(id:)`\\[cite: 1\\]. Reconstruct the active list from logs (`emailIntakeAddressCreated` minus `emailIntakeAddressDeleted`) and discard dead IDs\\[cite: 1\\].\n* Verify each address links to exactly one Team or one template (dual targets constitute a Finding)\\[cite: 1\\]. If linked to a template, verify `templateData.teamId` (falling back to the template's own Team if undefined)\\[cite: 1\\].\n* Confirm web forms and intake addresses route to the LCV Team Triage queue\\[cite: 1\\]. Note: Intelligent triage reclassification moving items out of Triage based on content is expected behavior; never disable it or revert processed items\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### D. Bilateral Linear ↔ GitHub Reconciliation & Ecosystem Sync\n\n* Synchronize status, priority, assignees, labels, and content across GitHub (Projects, Discussions, Issues, PRs, Releases), Linear (Issues, Projects, Teams, Initiatives, Cycles, Milestones), and Entire (Trails, Dispatches, Checkouts, Memorys)\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Do not link entities based solely on title similarity; PR edges are many-to-many\\[cite: 1\\].\n* Verify Linear GitHub App installation, Webhook Payloads, and Project Auto-add settings\\[cite: 1\\]. Commit linking must enforce JSON, SSL verification, and exclusively the `push` event\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Webhook & Link Rule:** Create external links strictly from Linear using `entityExternalLinkCreate` with explicit UUIDs (`projectId`)\\[cite: 1\\]. Never inject URLs into GitHub Projects v2 `readme` or `shortDescription` fields to simulate links\\[cite: 1\\]. If editing a Project v2 `readme` is required, fetch the full text first and overwrite in a single call\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Baselines:** `.github-private` has Discussions disabled; the remaining 16 org repositories use the 6 factory Discussions categories (valid state, not a finding)\\[cite: 1\\]. Projects target 1:1 repository boards; Portfolio #17 is deleted; Project #15 holds a valid historical baseline of 44 cross-repository cards (flag only if Project #15 exceeds 44 or cross-repo cards appear elsewhere)\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Write Consistency Policy:** Reread the target edge immediately prior to writing\\[cite: 1\\]. Execute at most one write per pass\\[cite: 1\\]. Due to Linear's eventual read-after-write consistency, do not repeat a write if an immediate reread returns the prior state; defer verification to the next independent audit pass\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### E. Projects, Cycles, Milestones & Metadata Hygiene\n\n* **Cycle Integrity:** Open Issues in flight (`Em Andamento`, `Em Revisão`, `A Fazer`) must possess a Priority, Label, Project, Team, and Cycle\\[cite: 1\\]. Issues in `Bloqueado`, `Triage`, or `Backlog` must NOT have a Cycle assigned\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Exclusions:** Exclude `completed`, `canceled`, and `duplicate` (`state.type`) when counting open Issues\\[cite: 1\\]. Never write to closed/archived records or the reserved `Duplicate` state\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Cycle Write Restrictions:** Validate against the baseline of 133 total Cycles (126 inherited, 7 writable in Team LCV; if live totals diverge, adopt the live count and log the date)\\[cite: 1\\]. Verify Team LCV ownership before writing, and enforce the strict $\\\\le 255$-character limit on Cycle descriptions\\[cite: 1\\].\n* **Empty Field Rule:** Populate empty metadata fields on open records (authorized additive write)\\[cite: 1\\]. If a field is already populated but diverges from expectations, do not overwrite it—log it as a finding\\[cite: 1\\]. Log non-writable fields or platform refusals as unobservable surfaces\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n### F. Entire Session Capture Recovery\n\nIf any agent session (`Codex`, `Claude Code`, `Copilot CLI`, `Antigravity`) failed to link to an Entire checkpoint on a published, signed commit\\[cite: 1\\]:\n\n1. Identify the agent and session via `entire agent list` and `entire session current --json`, verifying registration in `.entire/settings.local.json`\\[cite: 1\\].\n2. Diagnose via `entire status --detailed` and `entire doctor` (checking for execution from parent workspace directories instead of the repository root)\\[cite: 1\\].\n3. Confirm the local commit SHA matches the remote branch via `git log -1 --show-signature --format=fuller` and `git ls-remote`\\[cite: 1\\]. Never attach to an unpublished commit if it risks altering the SHA or invalidating the cryptographic signature\\[cite: 1\\].\n4. Execute `entire session attach <SESSION_ID> --agent <AGENT_ID> --commit <FULL_COMMIT_SHA> --force`\\[cite: 1\\].\n5. Validate readback: confirm pre- and post-attach SHAs are identical, the signature remains intact, and metadata pushed to origin (`git ls-remote origin | Select-String -SimpleMatch \"<CHECKPOINT_ID>\"`)\\[cite: 1\\].\n\n## 5. HARD COMPLETION LOCK & IRREFUTABLE PROOF OF IMPOSSIBILITY\n\n* **MANDATORY RESOLUTION LOCK:** You are strictly forbidden from closing or concluding this audit as fully resolved (`PASS_ZERO_WRITE` or `PASS_APPLIED`) unless it is **irrefutably proven** with concrete live evidence (UUIDs, full SHAs, node IDs, readback payloads) that **zero unresolved pendencies remain** across the entire fleet.\n* **BURDEN OF PROOF FOR UNRESOLVED ITEMS (**`PARTIAL` **/** `STOPPED`**):** You are prohibited from declaring any item \"pending\", \"inconclusive\", \"missing\", or \"blocked\" based on summaries, empty basic searches, or generic access errors\\[cite: 1\\]. To declare an audit with open pendencies, you must **irrefutably prove that resolution is technically impossible** under current constraints by executing and logging all of the following:\n  1. Exhaustive search across official docs, forums, and the Internet Archive\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n  2. Three (3) distinct, documented remediation attempts for the exact same root cause, providing raw error payloads, exact SHAs, workflow/job/step IDs, and secret-free reproduction logs\\[cite: 1\\].\n  3. If blocked by a third-party bug, a public Issue opened on the upstream repository containing a minimal reproduction and complete logs (or a complete technical draft prepared for GitHub Support)\\[cite: 1\\].\n  4. If blocked by API rate limits (`QUOTA_ESGOTADA`), you must verify and prove the exact quota exhaustion and Brasília reset timestamp using:\n\n     ```bash\n     gh api rate_limit --jq '{graphql: .resources.graphql, core: {remaining: .resources.core.remaining, limit: .resources.core.limit}}' && node -e \"const r=\\$(gh api rate_limit --jq '.resources.graphql.reset'); const d=new Date(r*1000); const br=new Date(d.getTime()-3*3600*1000); console.log('Reset GraphQL:', br.toISOString().slice(11,19), 'Brasilia — em', Math.ceil((r*1000-Date.now())/60000), 'min');\"\n     ```\n\n     Log the exact reset date/time from the native response, discard pure quota exhaustion as a system defect, and do not open tracking Issues for pure quota blocks\\[cite: 1, 2\\].\n\n## 6. COMMUNICATION, REPORT CONTRACT & CLOSURE\n\n* **LANGUAGE & FORMATS:** Internal reasoning must occur in your native language; all output directed to the operator must be in **Brazilian Portuguese (pt-BR)** using standard Brazilian date/time formats (`DD/MM/AAAA HH:MM:SS`), except for the three mandatory English section headers below\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Deliver the report directly with zero preambles or conversational filler\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\].\n* **MANDATORY REPORT STRUCTURE:** Do not generate cluttered side files\\[cite: 1, 2, 3\\]. Output a single consolidated report using **exclusively** these three English headings\\[cite: 1\\]:\n\n  ### Linked now\n\n  \\[List resources corrected, links created, Project/Team, edge key, previous state, operation, returned ID/URL, readback verification, and coverage\\]\\[cite: 1\\]\n\n  ### Already linked\n\n  \\[List resources verified as compliant with concrete live-state evidence and zero writes\\]\\[cite: 1\\]\n\n  ### Real failures\n\n  \\[Grouped by severity: `CRITICAL`, `HIGH`, `MEDIUM`, `LOW`, or `OBSERVABILITY`. Include run ID, workflow/job/step, SHA, secret-free payload, literal error, impact, tracking Issue, and irrefutable proof of blocker/impossibility\\]\\[cite: 1\\]\n* **METRIC CONCLUSION & LOCK RELEASE:** Conclude with explicit metadata blocks for `CONFIGURATION` (`MODO`, `RUN_KEY`, time window), `TOTALS` (section counts and effective writes across GitHub, Linear, and Slack), and `GLOBAL RESULT` (`PASS_ZERO_WRITE`, `PASS_APPLIED`, `PARTIAL`, or `STOPPED`)\\[cite: 1\\]. Dispatch exactly one consolidated notification to `#linear-activity` in Slack reflecting verified Project Updates (zero duplicate fallbacks), release the shared reconciliation lock, and close the execution Issue (if and only if zero actionable pendencies remain)\\[cite: 1\\].",
